# LIQUID-10 — Prefer section settings over hardcoded global references

## Rationale

Hardcoded metafield namespaces, settings keys, or collection handles make themes
inflexible and harder to maintain. Section and block settings with dynamic
references (collection pickers, metafield references, richtext) let merchants
configure content without code changes.

## How to check

Look for hardcoded `product.metafields.*`, `settings.*` feature toggles tied to
specific keys, or literal collection handles like `collections['featured-products']`.

## How to fix

Expose content sources via `{% schema %}` settings/blocks — collection pickers,
product metafield references, richtext fields — and read from
`section.settings` / `block.settings` in the template.

## Examples

### Bad

```liquid
{% if product.metafields.main.subcopy != blank %}
  {{ product.metafields.main.subcopy | metafield_tag }}
{% endif %}

{% if collections['featured-products'].handle == collection.handle %}
  <div class="featured-badge">Featured Product</div>
{% endif %}
```

### Good

```liquid
{% if section.settings.subcopy_content != blank %}
  {{ section.settings.subcopy_content }}
{% endif %}

{% if section.settings.show_featured_badge %}
  <div class="featured-badge">
    {{ section.settings.featured_badge_text | default: 'Featured Product' }}
  </div>
{% endif %}
```

Add corresponding settings in `{% schema %}`.
